Description:
   Generate a sponsors.yml file for a given event.
   If the file already exists, adds the sponsor in the correct tier.
   If the sponsor already exists in the file, updates the existing sponsor record.
   Tiers can only be added on the first pass.

   Sponsors reference an organization in data/organizations.yml by slug. Pass --slug for an
   organization that is already there, or --name (with --website and --logo_url) to add it.

Example: Create a new sponsors.yml file for an event with the first sponsor added.
    bin/rails generate sponsors --event rails-world-2026 --tiers "Platinum,Gold,Silver,Sponsors,Members" \
      --name "AppSignal" --website "https://www.appsignal.com" \
      --logo_url "https://rubyonrails.org/assets/images/logo-appsignal.svg" \
      --tier "Platinum"

    This will create:
        /data/rails-world/rails-world-2026/sponsors.yml
    and add AppSignal to data/organizations.yml when it isn't there yet.

Example: Add a known organization to an existing sponsors.yml file
  bin/rails g sponsors --event rubyconf-austria-2026 --slug teamtailor --tier "Gold Online"

Example: Update a sponsor's tier or badge
  bin/rails g sponsors --event tropical-on-rails-2026 --slug appsignal --tier "Platinum" --badge "Wifi Sponsor"
